                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This has some big differences to the old demo I played back as a Kid on the 3Ds. I got the game for nostalgia. \r\n\r\nI do not recall the womens chests being.. large in the nintendo version. Turns out, they weren't! The art is DIFFERENT for that version and much more tame/kid friendly. PLUS I Learned later there is an ability that melts armor (which is neat in theory for combat) but also melts clothes and thus has weird undertones and stuff... Uncomfortable. I avoid using this ability so I am not sure how far it goes other than what I looked up.\r\n\r\nSeems some of the challenge levels might also require it given enemies for example the leader of the thief village thing that has a 1% catch rate but massive attacks that instakill, so without using the ability it seems intentionally difficult to get certain slimes from challenge levels and so on. \r\nAside from the weird creepy slime ability and strange undertones it is/can be a good strategy rpg. However it is not what I remember and I am very disappointed in how the game depicts its characters.\r\n\r\nI'd rather just take the time to over level slimes to stomp enemies than use the \"intended\" routes. Gross.",
